  "force_reason": "THREE changes, each measured. (1) MIGRATED PRICE BASIS: cfbenchmarks BRTI index plus the venue's own floor_strike, per C1, +0.0033 log loss at t +5.71 over 42 of 50 folds. The live path can now honour it: score_live passes the venue strike into build_windows BEFORE build_features, so all ten strike-derived features share one reference instead of the strike being patched onto the scored frame afterwards, where it reached only z_score. The trader is restarted onto --venue cfbenchmarks --strike-source venue immediately after this installs; until that restart the new artifact scores on the old basis, a ~1bp mismatch for at most one window. (2) SAMPLE REPAIR: the installed artifact trained on 18,797 rows with peer_quote_sources empty, so --quote-sources discarded the Polymarket gamma backfill and took most cross_venue rows with it; with --peer-quote-sources all and the implied_vol available_time repair the complete-cases sample is about 164k. (3) implied_vol DROPPED: its leave-one-out delta at ensemble_size 5 is +0.000017, inside the band of five independent noise draws (-0.000034 to -0.000007, |max| 0.000034), so it contributes nothing this design can measure, while costing 35% of the sample. cross_venue is KEPT although it also fails the pre-registered rule at t +2.63 against a 2.7 bar: its delta is 4.5x the noise floor and dropping it is a sample-versus-skill tradeoff that PREREG_ABLATION_20261022.md says needs its own test. The 2.7 threshold was NOT relaxed to admit it. vol_state, microstructure, offset and book_quote are all inside the noise band but constrain no rows, so they are kept rather than selected on noise. Bankroll is the measured shard-2 balance, 458.75.",
  "force_reason_correction": "CORRECTION, appended 2026-10-22 after reading the installed artifact's provenance. The reason above blames the replaced model's 18,797-row training sample on `peer_quote_sources` being empty, and claims this run repaired it by passing `--peer-quote-sources all`. That is WRONG in both halves. `scripts/_common.py` maps `--peer-quote-sources all` to an EMPTY tuple, so `[]` is the FIXED state and means 'do not filter the peer'; the broken state is `None`, which means the flag was never given. The replaced artifact 20261021T100526Z also recorded `peer_quote_sources: []`, so it already carried that fix and the Polymarket gamma backfill was never discarded from it. This run's `[]` is not a repair, it is the same value. The sample DID grow, 18,797 -> 154,812 rows and 4,836 -> 24,755 windows, and that part stands. The cause is the CANDLE QUOTE BACKFILL completed earlier the same day, which extended quote coverage from 2026-08-25, the live era alone, back to 2025-12-10. Under `--complete-cases` every training row needs a quote, so the earliest quote bounds the sample: measured, candles begin 2025-12-10 22:09 and no other quote source reaches earlier. Nothing else in the reason is affected. The migrated price basis, the implied_vol drop, keeping cross_venue, the untouched 2.7 threshold and the 458.75 bankroll are all as stated.",
